WEBVTT

00:03.211 --> 00:06.004
<i>Causes of death are many and varied.</i>

00:06.005 --> 00:09.591
<i>Old age, suicide, illness...</i>

00:09.592 --> 00:14.180
<i>But the cause of death that scares
the most people in this day and age...</i>

00:18.101 --> 00:19.269
<i>...is death by fire.</i>

00:40.915 --> 00:41.957
Careful!

00:41.958 --> 00:43.042
The sea's raging!

00:43.626 --> 00:45.336
H-Hey! Look there!

00:45.837 --> 00:48.214
Hey, now! What the heck is that?!

00:50.133 --> 00:52.594
What the heck is going on?

00:57.140 --> 00:58.557
<i>Breaking news.</i>

00:58.558 --> 01:02.478
<i>A giant pillar has appeared
in the Pacific Ocean.</i>

01:02.479 --> 01:04.897
<i>It seems to be
approximately 500 meters tall.</i>

01:04.898 --> 01:07.358
<i>Investigations into it are ongoing.</i>

01:07.859 --> 01:10.737
One giant pillar...

01:11.529 --> 01:15.200
There wasn't only one pillar
in the basement of the convent.

01:15.867 --> 01:17.285
This isn't the last one.

01:18.495 --> 01:20.497
Seven more will likely appear.

01:22.207 --> 01:25.418
Once all eight are out...

01:31.883 --> 01:34.803
The Great Cataclysm has begun...

03:11.858 --> 03:14.359
The first pillar has appeared.

03:14.360 --> 03:17.614
Yes. This marks the beginning.

03:18.323 --> 03:22.367
The Evangelist will issue orders again.
Stand by until they do.

03:22.368 --> 03:23.494
<i>Látom</i>.

03:27.373 --> 03:29.626
What is the matter, Lady Inca?

03:32.587 --> 03:35.297
Looks like that's it for today.
Let's go back.

03:35.298 --> 03:38.009
Oh, yes, Lady Inca.

03:39.594 --> 03:41.471
Looks like he's gone too.

03:42.096 --> 03:44.807
Great Cataclysm Executor Faerie...

03:48.978 --> 03:51.813
Captain Obi, shouldn't we be
on the scene as well?!

03:51.814 --> 03:55.276
We are wanted criminals.
We should not act rashly.

03:55.944 --> 03:57.111
But...

04:06.913 --> 04:07.789
What now?!

04:17.382 --> 04:18.465
What the heck is that?!

04:18.466 --> 04:20.760
Is that an Infernal?!

04:25.890 --> 04:27.557
It's coming this way!

04:27.558 --> 04:28.934
Run for it!

04:28.935 --> 04:30.895
BREAKING NEWS

04:31.854 --> 04:33.355
<i>Breaking news!</i>

04:33.356 --> 04:36.942
<i>Reporters on the scene
report that a massive</i>

04:36.943 --> 04:38.694
<i>Infernal has appeared in the Pacific Ocean</i>

04:38.695 --> 04:41.613
<i>under the giant pillar.</i>

04:41.614 --> 04:43.908
<i>The Fire Defense Agency has issued
orders to evacuate...</i>

04:44.492 --> 04:46.369
<i>What the heck is that?!</i>

04:46.953 --> 04:50.372
If that Infernal hits shore,
it's going to destroy everything!

04:50.373 --> 04:54.961
Captain Obi! I can reach the pillar
before it reaches shore on my feet!

04:55.628 --> 04:59.007
No one else here
can fight it while it's at sea!

05:00.008 --> 05:01.634
Please let me go!

05:04.971 --> 05:06.097
Okay.

05:10.685 --> 05:12.937
It's in your hands, Shinra.

05:14.439 --> 05:18.860
<i>Emergency vehicles are now
passing through.</i>

06:07.241 --> 06:08.575
<i>All units in position!</i>

06:08.576 --> 06:11.662
<i>Assume anti-naval formation MAT!</i>

06:12.205 --> 06:13.081
On the double!

06:17.877 --> 06:19.544
Get in position!

06:19.545 --> 06:21.254
MAT formation! In position!

06:21.255 --> 06:22.548
Aligning sights!

06:25.510 --> 06:29.013
That's a lot of war-ragged folks.

06:29.514 --> 06:33.142
There was no need for me to come
if the 2nd was going to come.

06:33.684 --> 06:38.105
That looks like a big,
strong kaiju from some kaiju movie.

06:38.106 --> 06:40.274
I don't care to do it.

06:41.442 --> 06:43.193
What are you talking about?

06:43.194 --> 06:46.238
You're a corporate soldier. It's your job.

06:46.239 --> 06:49.533
Very well, Director Oguro.

06:49.534 --> 06:53.662
You managers use every excuse in the book
to force your subordinates to work.

06:53.663 --> 06:58.250
An excuse? Is an order to defend
the country an excuse?

06:58.251 --> 07:01.044
I like picking on the weak, so for me,

07:01.045 --> 07:05.633
any reason that forces me to fight
something strong is an excuse.

07:10.721 --> 07:14.057
I'll do it. If it reaches the shore,

07:14.058 --> 07:18.061
all the stupid weaklings
that I love will die first.

07:18.062 --> 07:21.982
Yes, do it. I'm unpowered.

07:21.983 --> 07:25.444
You only take orders from me and the CEO.

07:25.445 --> 07:28.947
That's why I'm putting myself
in danger out here.

07:28.948 --> 07:32.701
One day, I'll get promoted
and start ignoring your orders too.

07:32.702 --> 07:35.037
Good, that's the spirit, Kurono.

07:35.621 --> 07:39.834
But by the time you get
promoted, I'll be an exec.

07:41.836 --> 07:44.504
What are the elites
from Haijima doing here?

07:44.505 --> 07:46.089
Are they famous or something?

07:46.090 --> 07:50.470
Director Oguro. He's a horrible man.
No one likes him.

07:51.387 --> 07:52.971
But he climbed the corporate ladder

07:52.972 --> 07:55.140
by always
producing better-than-perfect results

07:55.141 --> 07:58.477
that silence all complaints.

07:58.478 --> 08:02.648
Anyone under him in Haijima
has a guaranteed future.

08:08.529 --> 08:11.907
What the heck?!
It's even bigger than the reports!

08:11.908 --> 08:14.118
That thing's an Infernal?!

08:14.785 --> 08:16.078
Ready weapons!

08:18.372 --> 08:20.082
Aim weapons!

08:21.834 --> 08:22.710
Fire!

09:19.809 --> 09:20.851
Don't back down!

09:21.852 --> 09:22.687
Fire!

09:53.342 --> 09:55.885
There it is! I can see it!

09:55.886 --> 09:58.471
Stop them from attacking it, Shinra!

09:58.472 --> 10:00.849
It'll cause
unimaginable destruction to Tokyo!

10:00.850 --> 10:03.102
Cease fire!

10:24.582 --> 10:25.833
- No way!
- Not a scratch?!

10:50.566 --> 10:51.733
Captain!

10:51.734 --> 10:53.944
- Are you all right?!
- Yes.

10:54.528 --> 10:58.114
All standard weaponry is unusable
due to computer damage!

10:58.115 --> 11:00.241
80 percent of crewmen are injured!

11:00.242 --> 11:03.120
The enemy has sustained no visible damage.

11:06.290 --> 11:08.416
Excuse me! I'm sorry I'm late!

11:08.417 --> 11:10.628
You're here, Juggernaut.

11:12.004 --> 11:15.800
It is only natural. You are
not used to your new leg yet.

11:16.300 --> 11:18.302
- Assume position!
- Yes, sir!

11:19.011 --> 11:21.639
So that is the 2nd's Takeru Noto?

11:22.306 --> 11:24.974
Direct support fire in position!

11:24.975 --> 11:27.186
- Preparations?
- Complete!

11:28.521 --> 11:30.063
You've grown strong.

11:30.064 --> 11:33.358
I can't just wait for
someone else to do it for me.

11:33.359 --> 11:37.487
If I don't fight,
I'll lose what's important to me!

11:37.488 --> 11:39.240
Aim weapons!

11:39.949 --> 11:41.616
Target locked!

11:41.617 --> 11:44.370
Deploy anti-cannon shockwave anchors!

11:45.121 --> 11:47.081
Anti-cannon shockwave anchors deployed!

11:48.416 --> 11:50.333
All preparations to fire complete!

11:50.334 --> 11:52.586
Fire!

11:53.838 --> 11:54.672
Don't!

11:55.297 --> 11:56.173
Shinra-kun?!

12:22.366 --> 12:24.951
Sh-Shinra-kun?!

12:24.952 --> 12:26.703
Why did he enter the line of fire?

12:26.704 --> 12:28.163
Don't break it!

12:28.164 --> 12:29.664
S-Scop-kun?!

12:29.665 --> 12:32.333
You can't fire anything at that pillar!

12:32.334 --> 12:34.127
Shinra was protecting the pillar!

12:34.128 --> 12:36.839
Huh? What do you mean?

12:37.673 --> 12:40.300
No, right now, we need to save Shinra-kun!

12:40.301 --> 12:42.887
Hey, wait! What are you doing?

12:43.971 --> 12:45.763
What are you doing, Juggernaut?

12:45.764 --> 12:48.808
In that equipment, you'll sink
to the seafloor!

12:48.809 --> 12:50.186
But...

12:54.440 --> 12:57.026
Kurono will save Kusakabe-kun.

13:00.362 --> 13:03.948
<i>Drowning victims are
something to watch and enjoy.</i>

13:03.949 --> 13:06.410
<i>Why do I have to save one?</i>

13:06.994 --> 13:08.495
Haijima...

13:08.496 --> 13:11.164
I haven't heard
anything good about that man.

13:11.165 --> 13:15.544
There is no better employee,
as long as he listens to you.

13:22.468 --> 13:28.015
<i>Shinra-kun,
you're still so weak. I'm glad.</i>

13:42.321 --> 13:46.033
Big and strong things aren't cute.

13:57.670 --> 14:00.296
At this rate, I'll be in trouble too.

14:00.297 --> 14:01.839
Do I drop my baggage?

14:01.840 --> 14:03.466
Kurono!

14:03.467 --> 14:07.596
If you abandon Kusakabe-kun,
it's coming out of your paycheck!

14:11.642 --> 14:13.936
It'll get both of them without cover!

14:15.646 --> 14:18.273
- You can't attack the pillar!
- Why not?!

14:18.274 --> 14:21.902
That pillar acts like a plug
on an undersea volcano!

14:22.486 --> 14:24.863
If you shoot it and destroy the pillar,

14:24.864 --> 14:28.825
the magma underneath
will erupt and destroy Tokyo!

14:28.826 --> 14:31.370
What?! But then...

14:33.414 --> 14:36.291
<i>My summer bonus... Demotion...</i>

14:36.292 --> 14:38.085
<i>That's bad.</i>

14:40.087 --> 14:44.967
<i>But my life is more important.
Perhaps I should drop him.</i>

14:51.932 --> 14:54.310
That's a good one, Juggernaut!

14:59.106 --> 15:05.029
If I fire from this pier and curve
the trajectory, I won't hit the pillar!

15:20.878 --> 15:22.420
Where's Kusakabe-kun?

15:22.421 --> 15:24.757
You didn't drop him, did you?

15:25.549 --> 15:27.592
I have him in tow.

15:27.593 --> 15:30.094
Hey! Get a medic here at once!

15:30.095 --> 15:31.763
You could at least pull me up.

15:31.764 --> 15:33.432
My suit will get wet.

15:35.392 --> 15:38.770
It isn't over yet. This is when it begins.

15:38.771 --> 15:40.147
I know that.

15:47.780 --> 15:49.239
How hard is it?

15:49.823 --> 15:54.202
It received that much fire and hasn't
moved an inch. It's impossible for me.

15:54.203 --> 15:56.664
Then do you want to take me on instead?

16:06.298 --> 16:08.550
Obviously not.

16:13.180 --> 16:15.474
That should take care of that.

16:16.058 --> 16:19.978
I got a wanted criminal too.
I didn't expect this nice bonus.

16:19.979 --> 16:21.312
What do you plan to do?

16:21.313 --> 16:23.272
He is a Fire Soldier.

16:23.273 --> 16:25.191
The 2nd and the army
will take him into custody.

16:25.192 --> 16:28.444
We at Haijima
already took him into custody.

16:28.445 --> 16:32.156
Your corporation intends to interfere
with the army's public duty?

16:32.157 --> 16:35.411
No, we will take him.

16:36.120 --> 16:38.746
Who are you? What is going on?

16:38.747 --> 16:41.583
For me, that is currently the ceiling.

16:48.549 --> 16:49.925
Kurono!

16:50.592 --> 16:54.303
Perfect. If I leave you,
that's one less strong superior.

16:54.304 --> 16:58.182
I filed with insurance so that if anything
happens to me on the job today,

16:58.183 --> 17:00.519
you bear responsibility
for work-related injury!

17:06.859 --> 17:08.985
You filed that with insurance?

17:08.986 --> 17:11.821
You understand
why all your subordinates hate you, right?

17:11.822 --> 17:14.908
It isn't my job to make
my subordinates like me.

17:23.125 --> 17:25.294
My suit's all covered in soot.

17:25.961 --> 17:28.087
That's one point down
on your performance review.

17:28.088 --> 17:30.423
Why? I saved you.

17:30.424 --> 17:34.093
Talk back again, and I'll
knock it down two points.

17:34.094 --> 17:36.346
Hurry and get Kusakabe-kun back.

17:40.309 --> 17:44.562
If I save him, will you reconsider
the performance review?

17:44.563 --> 17:46.647
I do not negotiate with subordinates.

17:46.648 --> 17:49.818
I'm only here to make sure
you don't make any wrong decisions.

17:50.819 --> 17:51.820
Do as I say.

17:55.157 --> 17:57.493
Yes, I know that.

18:04.500 --> 18:07.878
Now, stop the Titan. The time has come.

18:08.545 --> 18:12.132
Humans possess that power.

18:14.218 --> 18:16.719
Captain, are you all right?

18:16.720 --> 18:18.097
- Yes.
- What's that?!

18:21.600 --> 18:24.436
It seems to be absorbing something.

18:25.687 --> 18:27.314
What's going on now?

18:30.067 --> 18:32.276
It couldn't be... That's...

18:32.277 --> 18:35.614
Oh, no! The residents
are still evacuating from the plaza!

18:40.160 --> 18:42.745
Civilians, evacuate this way!

18:42.746 --> 18:44.414
Don't stop! Keep going!

18:52.673 --> 18:54.049
No!

19:05.435 --> 19:07.353
Eight buildings in the port are on fire!

19:07.354 --> 19:08.479
One is half-destroyed!

19:08.480 --> 19:13.402
Damages to the evacuating civilians and
2nd crewmen are under investigation!

19:14.528 --> 19:17.113
- Just get the medics to them immediately!
- Yes, sir!

19:17.114 --> 19:19.783
It just spat fire!

19:21.118 --> 19:23.912
All those great weaklings just died.

19:25.956 --> 19:27.666
What a disaster...

19:37.176 --> 19:38.217
Are you injured?

19:38.218 --> 19:39.552
N-No.

19:39.553 --> 19:43.181
I'm glad I made it.
Now, let's get out of here.

19:43.182 --> 19:44.933
No, I can't.

19:46.101 --> 19:47.768
Huh? It isn't hot?

19:47.769 --> 19:49.770
How am I still alive?

19:49.771 --> 19:51.898
You're right. The flames aren't hot.

19:51.899 --> 19:54.609
It's a defensive buff.
It won't be hot for a while.

19:54.610 --> 19:56.110
Now, let's go while it lasts.

19:56.111 --> 19:59.198
Captain Pan! Ogun's boss!

19:59.781 --> 20:01.617
The 4th came as well?

20:04.161 --> 20:06.788
Confirmed that the civilians
are unharmed! No injured!

20:07.789 --> 20:10.374
All right! That means we got no dead!

20:10.375 --> 20:11.542
This is the 4th!

20:11.543 --> 20:16.797
I'm changing your job description.
Defeat that Titan with highest priority.

20:16.798 --> 20:18.425
All right, fine.

20:20.677 --> 20:22.220
The enemy is on the sea.

20:22.221 --> 20:24.555
Flight will be necessary
to put it to rest.

20:24.556 --> 20:26.682
That's where Ogun comes in.

20:26.683 --> 20:29.728
You can leave it to me.
Buff me up, both of you!

20:31.104 --> 20:33.439
Go! Go! Juggernaut!

20:33.440 --> 20:36.485
Keep going! Keep firing!

20:37.069 --> 20:40.738
Okay! Close in while Juggernaut's firing!

20:40.739 --> 20:41.657
Roger!

20:46.453 --> 20:48.246
Karin, ready?

20:48.247 --> 20:49.373
Anytime!

20:52.876 --> 20:56.588
Got it! Captain Pan's offensive buff!

20:57.172 --> 20:58.257
Scale Shield!

20:59.424 --> 21:01.717
Got it, Karin!

21:01.718 --> 21:03.970
Ogun-kun! The left shoulder!

21:03.971 --> 21:06.347
Damage should be concentrated
on its left shoulder!

21:06.348 --> 21:09.016
Okay, Juggernaut!

21:09.017 --> 21:11.436
Flamy Ink!

21:13.522 --> 21:14.398
Fourth!

21:15.440 --> 21:16.316
Force!

21:16.984 --> 21:17.859
Dunk!

21:21.822 --> 21:23.615
Yes!

21:24.283 --> 21:28.161
You see that, 2nd?
That's Ogun from the 4th!

21:34.167 --> 21:36.961
When viewed up close,
it has quite some damage.

21:36.962 --> 21:39.423
The results of the 2nd's cannon fire?

21:40.048 --> 21:40.882
If so...

21:45.971 --> 21:49.849
What is your man doing
attached to the Titan?

21:49.850 --> 21:52.686
He must've found a place
where he can pick on it.

21:55.731 --> 21:59.401
You must never show any weakness
to him under any circumstances.

22:00.277 --> 22:03.447
The moment you do, he'll tear you apart.

22:18.462 --> 22:19.546
Yes, good.

22:20.547 --> 22:24.718
The ritual cannot continue
unless the Titan is defeated.

22:38.023 --> 22:42.944
TO BE CONTINUED

24:14.536 --> 24:15.411
<i>Stay there and watch.</i>

24:15.412 --> 24:18.289
<i>The prelude
to the Great Cataclysm to come.</i>

24:18.290 --> 24:19.456
<i>Why you and me?</i>

24:19.457 --> 24:22.084
You fly so fast
that we go back to the past.

24:22.085 --> 24:23.002
And then...

24:23.003 --> 24:24.879
<i>Next time, "Ancient Madness."</i>

24:24.880 --> 24:27.465
<i>Return to the great flame of fire.</i> Látom.
